# E11c (pre-existing - db2af5d gives the same) x T25c (wt-qc): Str "must have no effect" - "$ calls it as often as
# building the text needs (measure, write, or never)" - and that is checked as K1a evaluability, which refuses a global
# write but not a write through a reference: a Str whose receiver (by value or by reference) holds a "mut" reference and
# writes through it is accepted. The built program then runs it twice per "$" (measure, then write) and -i once, so the
# modes disagree. With G an immutable global (and a by-value receiver) it is also a read-only copy written through,
# which T25c refuses for every explicit call (an operator, Eq, Hash, At, Len, Call ... all give error[T25c]) but not for
# the implicit Str call.
# expected: an error at Str (E11c: it writes through a reference) - or "b 1 b 1" in every mode
# actual:   -b and -d print "b 2 b 2" (G's counter written twice per "$"); -i prints "b 1 b 1"
type Ctr struct() {
    n I64 = 0
}
type B struct(c mut Ctr&) { c }
G B = B(Ctr())
fn (a B) Str() String {
    a.c.n = a.c.n + 1
    return "b"
}
fn main() ? {
    x := B(Ctr())
    s := $x
    t := $G
    print(s)
    print(" " $x.c.n " ")
    print(t)
    println(" " $G.c.n)
}
